{
  "_notes": [
    "Input for scripts/make_fixture.py. Copy this, swap the columns and rows for the new",
    "bank's, keep the variant list. Verified: pointed at the Sparkasse rows, this generator",
    "reproduces fixtures/sparkasse-camt-18{,-utf8,-utf8-bom}.csv byte for byte.",
    "",
    "quote: 'all-but-first' (Sparkasse leaves the first column bare), 'all', or 'minimal'.",
    "preamble: verbatim lines before the header, for banks that ship one (DKB, ING, Postbank).",
    "Row values are written verbatim. Put a real CRLF in a value to test an embedded newline",
    "and a real quote character to test quote doubling - a bare \\n here produces an LF the",
    "rest of the file does not have, which is the one mistake this generator cannot catch.",
    "Columns missing from a row render as empty fields. Every index — patch, onlyRows, blankAfterRow — counts rows in this file's shared 'rows' array, never the filtered result, and a patch that onlyRows would drop is an error rather than a silent no-op."
  ],
  "name": "examplebank-giro",
  "outDir": "fixtures",
  "delimiter": ";",
  "quote": "all-but-first",
  "preamble": [],
  "blankAfterRow": [2],
  "trailingBlank": false,
